{"id":160225905,"slug":"tardive-dyskinesia-do-i-have-it","title":"Tardive Dyskinesia: Do I Have It?","subtitle":"Owen Muir, M.D. Realizes He Has The Problem He Has Been Studying","post_date":"2025-04-03T22:58:51.429Z","audience":"everyone","type":"podcast","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/tardive-dyskinesia-do-i-have-it","wordcount":85,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:47:58.322Z","body_sha256":"5bfd0072771507c8d55152233f21bf098ff9c338cad625c1562b78ccccbd2401","text_words":89,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>Oh my.  The irony is thick with this one.  Your author, and sometimes scientist, Owen Scott Muir, M.D. has been doing research on Tardive Dyskinesia.   And…he might have the disorder.  The search function lets you search for other articles on the topic. </p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p>If you are interested in treatments for psychiatric disorders that don't cause this adverse effect—a permanent movement disorder—they exist.  The care we provide in New York, California, and now, South Carolina works, diligently, to advance the science of safer treatment.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://app.meetradial.com/fermata&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Explore Options at Fermata&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://app.meetradial.com/fermata\"><span>Explore Options at Fermata</span></a></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/